## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Type definitions for CAPA (illustrative)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  status: 'proposed'|'in_progress'|'implemented'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure region-aware metrics and dashboards?
- What RCAs templates and safeguards would you require before closing a CAPA?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a CAPA program for cross-tenant log exposure caused by race conditions in multi-region deployments.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, redaction configs, tenantId, logs
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link logs/traces
- Metrics: exposure rate, MTTR, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollout plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {tenantId, issue, evidence} = req.body;
  if(!tenantId || !issue) return res.status(400).send('bad input');
  // Persist CAPA skeleton (pseudo)
  res.status(201).send({id: 'capa-1', tenantId, issue});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune the policy?
- What synthetic tests ensure coverage across regions during canary rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?
